<figure class="viz" id="viz-stages">
  <p class="chart-title">Four stages, and a growing bet</p>
  <p class="stage-axis">Higher on the ladder, wider exposure. The bar lengths are a sketch of that argument.</p>
  <ol
    class="stage-ladder"
    aria-label="Four automation stages. Action implementation is at the top, with the widest exposure bar. Information acquisition is at the bottom, with the narrowest. The bars are a conceptual sketch of reward and risk exposure, not a measurement. The note on each stage is where a person still sits."
  >
    <li class="stage-top">
      <div>
        <p class="stage-kicker">4 · Action implementation</p>
        <p class="stage-name">Control and execution</p>
        <p class="stage-human">
          When the choice is already automated and a wrong move is costly, the person still makes the last movement.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="stage-meter">
        <span class="stage-meter-label">Widest exposure</span>
        <span class="stage-track"><span class="stage-fill" style="--fill: 100%"></span></span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div>
        <p class="stage-kicker">3 · Decision and action selection</p>
        <p class="stage-name">Action selection</p>
        <p class="stage-human">
          The machine may suggest one option. When the cost is high and a person may have to take over, the person still chooses.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="stage-meter">
        <span class="stage-meter-label">Wide exposure</span>
        <span class="stage-track"><span class="stage-fill" style="--fill: 74%"></span></span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div>
        <p class="stage-kicker">2 · Information analysis</p>
        <p class="stage-name">Information integration</p>
        <p class="stage-human">
          The machine combines and infers. High automation can be reasonable when it is reliable and the raw data stays available.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="stage-meter">
        <span class="stage-meter-label">Moderate exposure</span>
        <span class="stage-track"><span class="stage-fill" style="--fill: 48%"></span></span>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div>
        <p class="stage-kicker">1 · Information acquisition</p>
        <p class="stage-name">Information retrieval</p>
        <p class="stage-human">
          The machine senses and registers. High automation can be reasonable on those same terms, with a way back to the raw input.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="stage-meter">
        <span class="stage-meter-label">Narrow exposure</span>
        <span class="stage-track"><span class="stage-fill" style="--fill: 24%"></span></span>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption>
    A conceptual sketch: reward and the number of ways a risk can become an incident both grow from retrieval toward execution.
    The four stages, and where a person still sits, follow{' '}
    <a href="https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/844354/">Parasuraman, Sheridan, and Wickens, 2000</a>.
    The bar lengths are illustrative.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
